course: dictionary
lesson: 1510
title: Words for places
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A cellar is a room under a house or building, below the ground. It is often cool and dark, and people use it to store things like coal, food, tools and old things.
explain: Context helps you work out what a word means. Look at the words around cellar: «The Rat comes back from the cellar with bottles of beer.» The word from tells you the cellar is a place you go into and come out of, and the bottles tell you it holds things to drink.
explain: Now test your meaning by swapping it in: «The Rat comes back from the room under the house with bottles of beer.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Wine cellars are places where wine is kept.
fact: A cellar is a room under a house or building, below the ground.
fact: A wine cellar is a place where wine is stored, or the wine itself.
fact: The phrase «from cellar to attic» means the whole house, from the bottom room to the top one.
fact: In places with tornadoes, people shelter in a storm cellar to stay safe.
fact: In French, «la cave» means cellar. A cave in a hill is «une grotte».
exercise: «The Rat comes back from the cellar with bottles of beer.» Where does the Rat get the bottles? | On the roof of the house | *In a room under the house | In a shop at the top of the street | In a cave in the hills
exercise: «Before fridges, people shopped often and kept food cool in cellars or with ice.» What were cellars used for here? | To hold parties on the roof | *To keep food cool | To watch films | To grow tall trees
exercise: What does the phrase «from cellar to attic» mean? | Only the garden | Just the kitchen | *The whole house | A long journey by train
test: A tornado is coming, so the family runs to the storm cellar. Where are they going? | Up a tall hill | Into the garden shed | *Underground, to a room below the ground | In the attic at the top of the house
test: Which word means a place where wine is stored? | cave | *wine cellar | garden | attic
exam: Which is correct: a cellar is | a tall tower on a hill | a type of tall tree | a small wooden boat | *a room under a house or building, below the ground
